        /* Was ".sidebar-card.active .card-content { display: block; }" here - that rule and the
           jQuery slideToggle() below (which the click handler at the bottom of this file uses to
           animate .card-content open/closed) were both trying to control the same element's
           display at once, and racing each other. toggleClass("active") applied synchronously,
           instantly making this CSS rule show the content; slideToggle(), reading the *now-already-
           visible* element a moment later, saw it as "already open" and animated it straight back
           closed - which is exactly the reported "quickly open and close instead of staying open"
           bug. slideToggle() already manages this element's display itself (that's the whole point
           of using it), so this rule only needs to control the chevron icon rotation now - removing
           it leaves slideToggle() as the single source of truth for whether the content is shown. */
        .sidebar-card.active .card-toggle i {
            transform: rotate(180deg);
        }
